From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] icu: the ICU functions programs import beyond the .NET list

Windows' icu.dll is a whole ICU build; icu.dll forwarded only the functions .NET binds. make_host.py now also forwards the names in app_names.txt: what Telegram Desktop (Qt) delay-imports -- case mapping, UTF-8, language tags, collation strength, the default time zone, number and date formatting with field positions, list, plural and relative-date formatters. The 32-bit side keeps their objects as handles and widens ulistfmt_format's array of strings.
---
--- a/dlls/icu/make_host.py
+++ b/dlls/icu/make_host.py
@@ -2,7 +2,8 @@
 """make_host.py [OUTDIR]: icu.dll's forwarders to the host ICU (host.c, unixlib.c, icu_host.h and
 host.spec, whose lines are in icu.spec) for the ICU C API .NET's System.Globalization.Native binds:
 the names in dotnet_names.txt (dotnet/runtime, MIT: pal_icushim_internal.h FOR_ALL_ICU_FUNCTIONS,
-.NET 5.0 through 10), with the prototypes of the host's ICU headers (/usr/include/unicode).
+.NET 5.0 through 10), then those in app_names.txt (what other programs import from icu.dll, wine-sg
+9800), with the prototypes of the host's ICU headers (/usr/include/unicode).
 
 Copyright (C) 2026 Stained Glass OS contributors; LGPL-2.1-or-later
 """
@@ -11,9 +12,11 @@
 out = sys.argv[1] if len(sys.argv) > 1 else here
 HANDLES = {'UCollator','UBreakIterator','UCalendar','UDateFormat','UDateTimePatternGenerator','UEnumeration',
            'UIDNA','UNormalizer2','UNumberFormat','UResourceBundle','UStringSearch','UCollationElements',
-           'ULocaleDisplayNames'}
+           'ULocaleDisplayNames','UFieldPositionIterator','UListFormatter','UPluralRules',
+           'URelativeDateTimeFormatter'}
 NATIVE = {'u_strlen','u_strcmp','u_strcpy','u_strncpy'}   # plain string functions, in the PE side
-names = [l.strip() for l in open(os.path.join(here, 'dotnet_names.txt')) if l.strip() and not l.startswith('#')]
+names = [l.strip() for f in ('dotnet_names.txt', 'app_names.txt')
+         for l in open(os.path.join(here, f)) if l.strip() and not l.startswith('#')]
 text = ''
 for f in sorted(glob.glob('/usr/include/unicode/*.h')):
     text += open(f, errors='replace').read() + '\n'
@@ -32,6 +35,7 @@
     if args and args != 'void':
         for a in args.split(','):
             a = a.strip()
+            if a.endswith('[]'): a = re.sub(r'(\w+)\s*\[\]$', r'*\1', a)   # const UChar* const strings[]
             m = re.match(r'(.*?)(\w+)$', a)
             t, n = m.group(1).strip(), m.group(2)
             params.append((t, n))
@@ -149,6 +153,10 @@
